
# Where the browser asks for sponsorship. This is our own endpoint, not the
# provider's: a paymaster key spends real money and anything the browser holds
# is public — the bundle ships to every visitor, so a key in it can be read out
# of the JavaScript in a minute, open source or not.
#
# Leave this as-is. The proxy at frontend/api/paymaster.js holds the real key
# and refuses any request that would sponsor a call into a contract that is not
# ours, so the budget can only be spent on what it was funded for.
#
# Absent is a supported state: everyone simply pays their own fees, exactly as
# before. Sponsorship is an improvement on the normal path, never a requirement.
REACT_APP_PAYMASTER_URL=/api/paymaster

# NOTE FOR PREVIEW DEPLOYMENTS
# Vercel's Deployment Protection puts previews behind an SSO login, and that
# applies to /api/* as well as pages. The paymaster URL is fetched by the
# wallet's own signer domain, which has no Vercel session, so it receives a
# redirect to vercel.com/sso-api instead of our function — the request never
# arrives and nothing is logged, which looks exactly like the function not
# existing.
#
# To test sponsorship on a preview, either turn Deployment Protection off for
# that deployment, or append a protection-bypass token to the URL above.
# Production is unaffected.
